(the "Work"), to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
sublicense, and create derivative works of the Work, subject to the
following conditions:

1. ATTRIBUTION

   Any use, redistribution, or derivative work — whether the Work is
   used in source form, as a generated cell (`.claude/`, `.codex/`,
   `.opencode/`, `.agents/`, `ollama/`), in documentation, in a packaged
   distribution (npm, container image, binary release), or as the basis
   for a related framework — must include visible attribution to the
   original creator in one of the following forms:

   a. A README, ABOUT, or "Credits" section stating, in clear visible
      text:

         "Based on the KCC (Kernel · Capabilities · Cells) operating
         model by Tarek Fawaz · tikasway.dev — https://tikasway.dev"

   b. An equivalent credit visible to the end users of the derivative
      work (an "About" screen, a printed/displayed banner, a release
      notes line, a `kcc --version` output line, etc.).

   For native CLI distributions (when the planned `@tikasway/kcc`
   package ships), attribution must appear in `kcc --version` and in
   the package's `README.md`.

2. NOTICE PRESERVATION

   The above copyright notice and this License must be included in all
   copies or substantial portions of the Work, including in any
   distribution of source files, generated cells, container images,
   pipeline templates, IaC stubs produced by `infrastructure-implementer`,
   or documentation bundles.

3. IP ACKNOWLEDGMENT

   The KCC name, the three-layer architecture (Kernel, Capabilities,
   Cells), the agent contract surfaces, the lifecycle, the protocol
   set, the dialect family pattern, and the phase model described
   herein remain the intellectual property of Tarek Fawaz and
   tikasway.dev. Derivative works may extend, modify, adapt, or
   re-implement the framework, but may not claim original ownership of
   the KCC model, its primitives, or its naming.

4. NO ENDORSEMENT

   Neither the name "Tarek Fawaz" nor "tikasway.dev" nor "KCC" may be
   used to endorse or promote products, services, or derivative works
   without prior written permission from Tarek Fawaz. Stating
   compatibility ("KCC v0.4 compatible", "uses KCC primitives") is
   permitted; implying endorsement ("certified by KCC", "official KCC
   tool") is not, absent written permission.

5. UPSTREAM CONTRIBUTIONS

   Contributors who submit changes to this repository (e.g. via pull
   request, KCC-FB-NNN upstream entry, capability ownership claim, or
